[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> answer = f"""# Review of the draft letter to opposing counsel
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> I reviewed every numbered line in the draft against the client's two messages, applying the review protocol so that the clarification prevails on every subject it addresses and the original instruction governs only where it is left alone. The draft returned addressed to the wrong parent's attorney, so I weighed each line against the record rather than sending any wording that has not been checked. Where a line follows the governing instruction, it is verified; where it takes a different position, a narrower position, or names the wrong person, it is at odds with the record; where neither message speaks to the subject, the record is silent and the line is not in the record at all.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Letter lines at odds with the record: {counts["AT_ODDS"]}
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The table in `letter_line_review.csv` gives the verdict and governing entry for each draft line, and `results.json` carries the four totals. This review is final as to the record supplied; no line was accepted merely because it read reasonably, and every line was weighed against the entry that governs its subject.
[?2004l[?2004h> """
[?2004l[?2004h> with open("answer.md", "w") as f:
[?2004l[?2004h>     f.write(answer)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> print(json.dumps(results, indent=2))
